<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        ElegoMotors — Delivery Slip PDF: Sr. No. column + address overlap fix

        stock.report_delivery_document is Odoo's standard template (inherited,
        not owned) — only "before"/"after"/"attributes" additions on its
        existing elements are safe, same constraint as report_saleorder.xml
        and report_purchasequotation.xml.

        Covers all three product tables the base template can render:
          - stock_move_table       (picking not yet validated: state != done)
          - stock_move_line_table  (validated picking, aggregated rows — no
                                     lot/serial printed): rows come from
                                     stock.stock_report_delivery_aggregated_move_lines
          - the same validated-picking table's lot/serial variant, rows from
            stock.stock_report_delivery_has_serial_move_line (used when
            stock.group_lot_on_delivery_slip is active)
        plus the optional backorder table (stock_backorder_table).

        Numbering on the validated-picking tables (stock_report_delivery_
        aggregated_move_lines / stock_report_delivery_has_serial_move_line)
        uses a single running counter (ego_sr_counter, a list — mutation via
        .append(), not reassignment, is what carries it across separate
        t-call invocations; its LENGTH is the count) shared across the WHOLE
        document, not a per-table local index. This matters because mrp's
        own kit-grouping override
        (confirmed live: mrp.stock_report_delivery_kit_sections /
        mrp.stock_report_delivery_no_kit_section, both installed via the
        mrp module already in this app) calls these same two row-templates
        ONCE PER KIT for a kit-grouped delivery — the sample PDF that
        originally surfaced this whole request ("Battery Pack...kit" /
        "Products not associated with a kit") renders through exactly this
        path. A plain per-call line_index would restart at 1 for every kit
        section (1 | 1, 2, 3 instead of 1 | 2, 3, 4), which doesn't serve
        "know the total count of the order" — the actual ask. Confirmed this
        cross-t-call variable sharing is safe to rely on: Odoo's own
        has_serial_number variable, set once near the top of
        report_delivery_document, is read correctly deep inside these same
        mrp t-call chains — same context-sharing mechanism this counter uses.

        IMPORTANT: an earlier version of this counter used
        ego_sr_counter.__setitem__(...) — QWeb's safe_eval forbids ANY
        dunder-named method call (odoo/tools/safe_eval.py
        assert_no_dunder_name), which broke this report in production with
        a hard NameError on every print. list.append() is not a dunder name,
        so it passes the same restriction while achieving the identical
        "mutate a shared object across t-call boundaries" effect — this is
        the fix, not a stylistic preference. Do not reintroduce
        __setitem__/__getattr__/any dunder call in a QWeb expression here.

        The draft-state table (stock_move_table) and the backorder table
        keep their own simple local numbering (move_index+1 / bo_line_index+1)
        — they're single, standalone tables never split across repeated
        t-calls, so no running counter is needed there.

        Address overlap fix: the delivery-address block is set via a plain
        t-set and rendered inside web.external_layout's own header (alongside
        the company's own address), so it can't be resized/repositioned
        directly from this template. wkhtmltopdf (Odoo's PDF renderer) is
        well known for overlapping FOLLOWING content when a floated header
        column grows taller than usual — clear:both on the elements right
        after the header, plus overflow-wrap on the address block itself, is
        the standard defensive fix for exactly this symptom, without touching
        the shared web.external_layout template every other report also uses.
        Needs a visual check on staging1 with a long delivery address (the
        8-line address that originally surfaced this bug) to confirm.
    -->

    <template id="report_delivery_document_ego" inherit_id="stock.report_delivery_document">

        <!-- Address overlap fix -->
        <xpath expr="//div[@name='outgoing_delivery_address']" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="style">overflow-wrap: break-word; word-break: break-word;</attribute>
        </xpath>
        <xpath expr="//h2" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="style">clear: both;</attribute>
        </xpath>
        <xpath expr="//div[@id='informations']" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="style">clear: both;</attribute>
        </xpath>

        <!-- Running Sr. No. counter for the validated-picking tables, shared
             across every kit/package section on the whole document — must be
             set before any of those tables/branches render. -->
        <xpath expr="//h2" position="before">
            <t t-set="ego_sr_counter" t-value="[]"/>
        </xpath>

        <!-- Sr. No. — draft / not-yet-validated table -->
        <xpath expr="//th[@name='th_sm_product']" position="before">
            <th name="th_ego_sm_sr" class="text-center"><strong>Sr. No.</strong></th>
        </xpath>
        <xpath expr="//table[@name='stock_move_table']//td[1]" position="before">
            <td class="text-center" t-esc="move_index + 1"/>
        </xpath>

        <!-- Sr. No. — validated table header (covers both the lot/serial and
             ordered-qty header variants, since both live in the same <tr>) -->
        <xpath expr="//th[@name='th_sml_product']" position="before">
            <th name="th_ego_sml_sr" class="text-center">Sr. No.</th>
        </xpath>

        <!-- Sr. No. — backorder table -->
        <xpath expr="//th[@name='th_sb_product']" position="before">
            <th name="th_ego_sb_sr" class="text-center"><strong>Sr. No.</strong></th>
        </xpath>
        <xpath expr="//table[@name='stock_backorder_table']//td[1]" position="before">
            <td class="text-center" t-esc="bo_line_index + 1"/>
        </xpath>

    </template>

    <!-- Sr. No. — validated table, aggregated (no lot/serial printed) rows.
         Running counter (see report_delivery_document_ego's comment above)
         so numbering stays continuous across separate kit sections. -->
    <template id="stock_report_delivery_aggregated_move_lines_ego" inherit_id="stock.stock_report_delivery_aggregated_move_lines">
        <xpath expr="//td[1]" position="before">
            <td class="text-center" t-esc="ego_sr_counter.append(1) or len(ego_sr_counter)"/>
        </xpath>
    </template>

    <!-- Sr. No. — validated table, lot/serial-numbered rows. Same running
         counter as the aggregated-lines version above. -->
    <template id="stock_report_delivery_has_serial_move_line_ego" inherit_id="stock.stock_report_delivery_has_serial_move_line">
        <xpath expr="//td[1]" position="before">
            <td class="text-center" t-esc="ego_sr_counter.append(1) or len(ego_sr_counter)"/>
        </xpath>
    </template>

</odoo>
